Z||000003||batboy||04-27-2000||08:10 PM||||Maybe it's just part of the growing pains. The internet forums and chats are relatively new. Proper etiquette and socially acceptable good manners haven't keep up with the fast computer age of split second world-wide communication.<P>One reason is the casualness, which I like being able to chat with others while I'm unshaven and in my sweats, but this casualness promotes off the wall comments said without thinking that it might be read by hundreds or even thousands of people of all different backgrounds, nationality, etc.<P>An other reason is probably the anonymousness of the 'net. I'm sure everyone knew or knows someone who is mouthy and rude on the phone, but in person, rarely acts that way.<P>You folks that have kids know about growing pains and that kids will get into fights. Put the gloves on and duke it out, I don't give a bat's guano, but stay out of my topics.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BigBoyToys||04-27-2000||08:26 PM||||I would also agree.<P>Since I typically just lurk in the background and monitor rather than post or reply (as I'm sure many others do); and, not knowing exactly how this forum operates under the covers or what is possible. I would purpose that rather than you/we argue about the issues lets put out some alternatives to solution the obvious (even though seldom) need to moderate this community.<P>- could Cliff authorize certian mature members as alternate moderators?<P>- could we as a community either nominate then elect a recommended list of moderators?<P>- Maybe as a community we could nominate a set of conduct guidelines that the moderators could use to maintain order?<P>Naturally this would not be at all necessary if some members of this community would use some common sense, respect towards each other and lets not be so quick to read between the lines. But lets face it we are all just human and thus will always have things in common as well as differences.<P>Just a thought because it would be a shame to let such a decent community go to the dogs! You know the expression it only takes one rotten apple to ruin the basket. <BR> <BR>No Flames Intended and No Fingers Being Pointed<P>BBT||||reg||5
Z||000005||stimpy||04-27-2000||08:34 PM||||The only finger I'll point is at myself.  I did something that was otally uncalled for and completely devoid of class. I wish it could be undone, but the damage has been done and I am sure that feelings were hurt. I am not going to say that this was accidental, but in retrospect this obviously was a BAD IDEA.<P>One and all, please accept my apologies and bear with me as I attempt to grow up.  ||||reg||1
