Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||04-28-2000||04:52 AM||||Let me explain a few things here. The foremost reason I started this forum was to create a place that wouldn't be moderated to death by an overactive moderator. I've been on the <I>other</I> lists and I got sick and tired of the moderators that were enforcing their own values upon others. You had to play by their rules or you would get kicked off for the simplest of things. I happen to love my little Fiero and it p'd me off that I wasn't able to get valuable information from certain list-members anymore - just because the moderator thought he was out of line by asking a question about subwoofers, for instance.<P>This indeed is not my job but I do feel a responsibility to keep this forum up and running. I spend a lot of time making sure people can get information as painless as possible. I don't mind that at all. My knowledge of Fieros is nowhere near that of some members and this is my way of contributing to the Fiero community.<P>It is true that members have left the forum because of the bashing that has been going on lately. I receive email about that daily. But I also realise that that is something that can not be prevented. The only thing I can hope for is that it will be confined to the O/T section. I want the Technical Discussion and General Fiero Questions areas to be as clean and on-topic as possible. If people need to get information for their Fiero, they should be able to do so without having to wade through flame-wars. I don't mind the occasional flame-war in the O/T section at all because it doesn't interfere with the on-topic sections. That's the reason why I closed that thread - not because of its contents but because it didn't belong there.<P>I don't like the idea of moderators. I strongly feel that everybody has the right to speak out his opinion (within generally acceptable limits of course). Just look at me as the cleaning-lady (or janitor if you will). I try to keep the house clean, but I can't and won't tell the inhabitants how to live their lives.<P>I do ask everybody to consider this: the forum is taking up valuable webspace and bandwidth, which I pay for out of my own pocket. In fact, the forum is growing so much that I will upgrade the server so it won't interfere with other websites I'm hosting. Again, this is something I pay for myself since this isn't a commercial site and there's just no way I can let my company pay for this. I'm not asking for any donations, I'm just asking to treat the forum with the respect I think it deserves. The forum has proven to be a fun place to hang out. Let's keep it that way.<P>Oh, and one more thing. Could we please stop the "thank you Cliff, you're doing a great job" messages? It's making me feel uncomfortable.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> If this is a great forum it's because of you, not me!||||reg||1
Z||000014||DJRice||04-28-2000||09:08 AM||||I thought that Janitor thing was a joke, but apparently Cliff takes his forum duties very seriously.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||bHooper||04-28-2000||09:11 AM||||sounds good to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||batboy||04-28-2000||10:45 AM||||Yeah, what Cliff said! Right on!||||reg||1
Z||000017||DRH||04-28-2000||02:53 PM||||I have been reading this forum for almost a year and posting for several months. The only <B>real</B> problem I've seen was a few months ago when some clown registered several times and proceeded to post obsenities back and forth to himself. Cliff took care of that in short order.<P>I think that being unmoderated is one of the best things about this forum. I enjoy reading differing opinions. I also enjoy the atmosphere the irrelevant comments (jokes) in a serious post provide. Sometimes these discussions have deteriorated to name calling. Sometimes the jokes have gotten a little out of hand. I think these are  unfortunate side affects of allowing a diverse group of people to express their opinions freely. In my opinion it is a small price to pay. Remember you do have a scroll bar and a back button.<P>I do think that too often heated debates have popped up in the middle of someone's request for information. Maybe "taking it to the Off Topic Section" should become a more often used courtesy?<P>Just my .02 worth, David.<BR>||||reg||1
